<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Matches api/Biolog.Api/Biolog.Api.csproj's pinned TFM (BIO-FND-008), same as every prior
         BIO-BIO story. -->
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    No ASP.NET Core dependency, no NuGet package references. ProjectReference to BIO-BIO-001
    only - the same "direct reference to a plain, host-agnostic contracts library" shape every
    prior BIO-BIO story established (BiometricTemplate/IFingerprintProvider/IBiometricMatcher).

    The approved story also names BIO-BIO-002 (guided tenprint/single-finger enrolment) as a
    dependency, but deliberately NO ProjectReference exists to it here - the identical situation
    BIO-BIO-004's own csproj remarks already document: BIO-BIO-002's own
    IFingerprintEnrolmentRepository/FingerprintEnrolmentService are internal, Singleton-registered,
    and expose no bulk/enumerate query at all (only get-by-session-id), and captured templates
    live embedded in its own session aggregate, never published anywhere queryable across many
    people. Reaching into BIO-BIO-002's owned paths to add such a query is out of this story's
    write scope (governance/feature-path-ownership.json).

    Unlike BIO-BIO-004, this story does NOT reuse BIO-BIO-001's own IBiometricTemplateStore
    either - that store's own contract (Matching/IBiometricTemplateStore.cs) only supports
    "get every template for ONE (tenant, person)", never "enumerate every enrolled identity in a
    tenant", which a 1:N GALLERY search fundamentally needs. Extending that interface would
    modify BIO-BIO-001's own owned files, equally out of this story's write scope. This story
    therefore defines its own Domain/IFingerprintGalleryStore.cs - a deliberately SEPARATE
    concept from BIO-BIO-001's per-identity reference store, the same "search gallery distinct
    from a canonical per-identity reference store" architecture a production AFIS/1:N search
    system commonly uses anyway, not merely a workaround. See
    docs/features/bio-bio-006/README.md "Design decisions" for the full reasoning, including how
    the gallery gets populated (an explicit IndexAsync call, since no existing seam can
    auto-populate it without modifying another story's owned files).

    Deliberately NO ProjectReference to BIO-IDN-005 (duplicate review) or BIO-IDN-006 (RBAC)
    either: both expose only internal, Scoped-registered services with no PUBLIC entry point this
    story can safely reach for its own purposes (BIO-IDN-005's own DuplicateSignalSource.Biometric
    enum member anticipates a future story raising it, but DuplicateReviewService.RaiseOrAugmentAsync
    - the only method that could do so - is PRIVATE, not even internal, so no ProjectReference
    could reach it regardless). This story defines its own narrow
    Domain/IBiometricSearchPermissionGateway.cs (AC02) and its own self-contained duplicate
    review queue (AC03) instead; the real gateway implementation is an adapter in
    Biolog.Api.Modules.BioBio006Module wrapping BIO-IDN-006's already-registered
    PermissionService.ActorHasPermissionAsync, the same "narrow gateway + host-level adapter"
    shape every prior BIO-BIO story uses for its own tenant-scoped upstream dependency.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../../bio-bio-001/Biolog.Features.Biometrics/Biolog.Features.Biometrics.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- IFingerprintGalleryStore/InMemoryFingerprintGalleryStore,
         IFingerprintDuplicateReviewRepository/InMemoryFingerprintDuplicateReviewRepository and
         FingerprintSearchService are internal (BIO-IDN-001-QA-01's governance shape, mirrored by
         every prior BIO-BIO story). This is the explicit, auditable seam that grants Biolog.Api
         (DI registration in Modules/BioBio006Module.cs) and this feature's own test project the
         same access. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Api" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Features.FingerprintSearch.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
